Third-party components shipped with cheap-mem
---------------------------------------------

cheap-mem has no runtime dependencies (package.json "dependencies" is
empty, and stays empty). Its dashboard ships three third-party files
(three.js and two DM Sans font subsets) VENDORED into assets/ instead — a deliberate, named exception decided by
the owner on 2026-09-28 (docs/dashboard-port-2026-09-28.md, section 6.1),
so the one UI looks and moves exactly like its sibling's and nothing is
ever loaded from a CDN. test/packaging.test.mjs (VENDORED) lists every
vendored file by path; a further one cannot arrive without a line there.

  three.js r180 (assets/three/three-r180.min.js)
    Copyright 2010-2025 three.js authors
    MIT License — full text in assets/three/LICENSE.
    Unmodified upstream build; the only change is the one global the
    bundle exports (window.MemThree) and its header comment.

